{"_about":"Readings for the 56 South African places of the 2026-11-11 held-out test of the sowing-calendar rule, in the same shape as sa-climate-sites-2026-11-10.json: what the app's own fetchNasaPower returned that day, and the independent ERA5 2001-2020 daily-minimum record. These places were held back from the design of the rule merged on 10 November; two of them (Butterworth, Mossel Bay) failed one criterion (CP-103, open). Now that they have been seen they are REGRESSION evidence, not a held-out set. Gridded estimates, not weather stations.","_independentRecordCorrection":"CORRECTION, 11 November 2026 (independent review, CBR-02): the daily record was requested from the Open-Meteo historical archive WITHOUT a `models` or `cell_selection` parameter, so the provider's defaults applied. Its documentation says the default 'Best Match' combines ECMWF IFS (from 2017), ERA5 and ERA5-Land, picks a land grid cell of similar elevation and adjusts to the point's elevation. The responses do not say which model produced them. So this is a reanalysis-based gridded record of that kind, not 'ERA5 only at the nearest cell' as first described. The numbers are unchanged; the key is still called era5 because tests read it by that name. Raw responses, checksums and an offline check are in the evidence folder.","_evidence":"docs/audits/2026-11-11/evidence-calendar-holdout/ (places and criteria written before the data was fetched, harness, full outputs)","sites":[
